{
  "file": "crates/trust-but-verify/tests/support/stored_graph.rs",
  "item": "impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[node_content]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "This storage-only consumer must delegate load/store using node_path\n without resolving contents. Domain requires the callback, but invoking\n this guard would violate the no-content-read invariant of the test.\n Other graph fixtures exercise content resolution."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/support/stored_graph.rs#impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[node_content]` is acceptable.\n\n- **Form:** It is an explicit function with a body. Its fenced commentary gives a substantive reason, not just difficulty. The function is a deliberate `panic!` guard that tests must never reach.\n- **Claims match the source:**\n  - `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` delegate straight to the file storage using `self.node_path(node)`. `node_path` reads only the cached node data, never contents.\n  - `Domain` does require `node_content`; the trait declares it in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs`.\n  - The body panics with \"storage operations must not read graph contents\", which fits the stated no-content-read invariant.\n  - Other fixtures do resolve contents. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs` (`impl[Memory/Domain]/fn[node_content]`), `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs` (`impl[Memory/Domain]/fn[node_content]`) and `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs` (`impl[Application/Domain]/fn[node_content]`) all do.\n- **Scope:** The exception covers only this function's zero execution. It does not excuse the file threshold.",
